<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carolingian dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Carolingians, Carlovingians, Karlings</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Carolingian dynasty was a Frankish noble family named after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-martel">Charles Martel</a> and his grandson <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a>, descended from the Arnulfing and Pippinid clans of the 7th century. In the 8th century the family made the office of mayor of the palace hereditary and became the real power behind the Merovingian throne. In 751 the Merovingians were overthrown and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepin-the-short">Pepin the Short</a> was crowned king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a>. The dynasty reached its peak in 800 with Charlemagne's coronation as emperor; after his death in 814 the empire fragmented, leading towards the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>After a struggle, his son Charles Martel took control and laid the ground for the <b>Carolingian dynasty</b>.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/december-16">16 December in history</a></li></ul></section>
